  "claim_short": "arXiv 2406.13291 Bhattacharjee Nailwal Question 1.2 completely alternating rational sequences p(x) product(x+b_i) residues c_i. Candidate full solution likely valid: write r=beta+alpha x+sum c_i/(x+b_i), w(t)=sum c_i t^{b_i}. Then r(n) is completely alternating iff alpha>=0 and w(t) 0. For rational data the sign test becomes polynomial nonpositivity on [0,1] decidable by Sturm sequences. Example residues (-1,2,-1)...",
